The New NAO has the following patches:
  * menucolors, compiled with POSIX regex. The old NAO was
    compiled with GNU regex, and if you were using "Eidocolors"
    they need to be changed slightly by escaping { and } with \
  * sortloot, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?42
  * slightly modified dumplog, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?40
    The modification allows using unix timestamp in the
    dump filename, so NAO will save every dump to unique
    filename.
  * showborn & extinct, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?43
  * slightly modified hpmon, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?45
    With an added option to turn it off.
  * dgamelaunch mail (so you can send mail to players)
  * paranoid quit, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?44
  * slightly modified version of use_darkgray,
    http://bilious.homelinux.org/?205
  * showbuc, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?198
  * window edge, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?14
  * extended logfile, http://bilious.homelinux.org/?289
  * whereis-file user game tracking lifted from Sporkhack 

Also, NetHack has been compiled with autopickup exceptions,
and I fixed the Astral call (SC343-11), srand() prediction
and cream pie (C343-218) bugs.


The website doesn't yet function fully, because the files
are now organized differently inside the nethack playground,
but for now you can browse to http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/
to see user's rcfile, dumplogs and ttyrecs.

